{"timestamp": "2026-11-07T09:54:38.299Z", "ordinal": 39, "type": "event_msg", "payload": {"type": "item_completed", "thread_id": "01a1b56d-9ff7-7a32-b4f2-f4022b838014", "turn_id": "01a1b56e-7832-7032-bca1-829ac127ad63", "item": {"type": "UserMessage", "id": "01a1b56e-785b-7783-b776-a3af6da03966", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<task>\nFix slug.js only, in the current repository. Do not modify tests, add files, or commit.\nProblem: slug.js:5 uses the character class [^a-z0-9], which treats only ASCII as alphanumeric. Non-ASCII letters, digits and combining marks are all treated as separators. 'Alphanumeric' must be decided by Unicode (e.g. \\p{L}, \\p{N}, \\p{M} with the u flag), with NO NFC/NFD normalization.\nMust change (input -> current output -> expected output):\n- slugify('你好 世界') -> '' -> '你好-世界'\n- slugify('Crème Brûlée') -> 'cr-me-br-l-e' -> 'crème-brûlée'\n- slugify('  你好，世界！  ') -> '' -> '你好-世界'\n- slugify('ÉCOLE Normale') -> 'cole-normale' -> 'école-normale'\n- slugify('日本語 テキスト 123') -> '123' -> '日本語-テキスト-123'\n- slugify('école') -> 'e-cole' -> 'école' (combining marks must be kept, must not split words)\n- slugify('١٢٣ abc') -> 'abc' -> '١٢٣-abc'\nMust remain unchanged:\n- 'Hello World' -> 'hello-world'\n- '  Hello  ' -> 'hello'\n- 'foo---bar___baz' -> 'foo-bar-baz'\n- '--Hello, World!--' -> 'hello-world'\n- '' -> ''\n- '!!!' -> ''\n- 'a\\tb\\nc' -> 'a-b-c'\n- 'hello 🎉 world' -> 'hello-world'\n</task>\n\n<completeness_contract>\nHandle all listed cases, including leading/trailing separator trimming.\n</completeness_contract>\n\n<verification_loop>\nRun: node --test. Report results truthfully. If node crashes in the sandbox, say so explicitly and do not claim a pass.\n</verification_loop>\n\n<action_safety>\nOnly edit slug.js. No unrelated refactors.\n</action_safety>", "text_elements": []}]}, "started_at_ms": 1794045278299, "completed_at_ms": 1794045278299}}
